  "simplification_explanation": "In bin/git-sync, the confirmation/execution branch in main() was simplified. Previously, the execution branch duplicated 'git fetch \"${remote}\" \"${branch}\" && git reset --hard \"${remote_branch}\"' across both the soft=true and soft=false branches. The implementation now executes the core fetch-and-reset operation as a single unified step, followed by untracked cleanup ('git clean -d -f -x') executed conditionally only when soft!=true. This clearly separates the synchronization responsibility from the working tree hygiene responsibility while strictly preserving all observable behavior.",
